WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.058
 When you play music--

00:00:02.058 --> 00:00:04.866
[PLAYING GUITAR]

00:00:06.738 --> 00:00:09.610
--you're bringing light
into the darkness.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.010
[DRUMMING]

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.950
I want to teach
because I love watching

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.915
humans unfold their wings.

00:00:16.915 --> 00:00:19.600
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.435
We're here to get
people's attention.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:30.170
I'm giving you reference
to an attitude.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:32.170
Some people will say,
what kind of pedal

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:33.670
is that, or what
kind of strings,

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:35.753
or what kind of guitar,
or what kind of amplifier?

00:00:35.753 --> 00:00:38.950
No, it was soul, heart,
mind, body, and your vitals--

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.330
one note.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.450
And with that note,
people go, whoa!

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:46.244
[PLAYING GUITAR]

00:00:46.244 --> 00:00:48.910
If you don't stand like that, it
ain't going to sound like that.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.770
Before you put your
fingers on the fret,

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:58.140
visualize these strings from
your eyes to your heart.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.898
And then you play.

00:00:59.898 --> 00:01:02.766
[PLAYING GUITAR]

00:01:04.209 --> 00:01:05.690
Whew!

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:06.530
Watch out, world!

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:10.590
[MUSIC - SANTANA, "OYE COMO VA"]

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.760
The real musicians
make the ugliest

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.487
face to create the
most beautiful note.

00:01:15.487 --> 00:01:17.320
They're leaving Earth,
and like, the gravity

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.930
is pulling their
face like, raaggh.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:23.107
And if your face don't show
that you're making an effort,

00:01:23.107 --> 00:01:24.940
then you're not going
to touch the listener.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:28.570
[MUSIC - SANTANA, "OYE COMO VA"]

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:31.990
We tend to look for greatness
always in somebody else rather

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:32.770
than yourself.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:34.600
Go inside and get your sound.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.380
You can only go into
the heart by you

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.940
being vulnerable yourself.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.307
That's a whole other
level of musicianship.

00:01:44.307 --> 00:01:46.692
[PLAYING GUITAR]

00:01:50.031 --> 00:01:51.470
Hoo!

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:53.180
I'm Carlos Santana.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:55.750
This is my MasterClass.

